**New Evidence**
1. Regional diplomacy and de-escalation framing from the AU.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Communiqué sur la situation sécuritaire entre la République de Rwanda et la RDC","publisher":"African Union","publication_date":"2022-06-13","url":"https://au.int/fr/pressreleases/20220613/communique-sur-la-situation-securitaire-entre-la-republique-de-rwanda-et-la","claim":"The AU Commission chair called for an immediate end to violence and urged Rwanda and the DRC to resolve the dispute through dialogue and regional mechanisms, including President João Lourenço and the Nairobi process.","locator":"press release body","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary AU communiqué on the crisis and the recommended diplomatic path.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Exact mid-2022 regional-crisis context.","ruler_attribution":"Regional framing rather than direct presidential action, but it sets the diplomatic environment Tshisekedi operated in.","contrary_evidence":["The communiqué does not establish Tshisekedi's own choices; it records AU-level counsel and pressure."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.7","2B.10"]}

2. Early June regional-force decision and no-Rwanda-deployment line.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Conclave de Nairobi : déploiement imminent de la force régionale sans l'armée rwandaise","publisher":"Présidence RDC","publication_date":"2022-06-20","url":"https://www.presidence.cd/actualite-detail/actualite/conclave_de_nairobi_deploiement_imminent_de_la_force_regionale_sans_larmee_rwandaise","claim":"At the Nairobi conclave, the participating heads of state approved the imminent deployment of a regional force in eastern DRC, and the communiqué said Rwandan troops would not be deployed on Congolese soil.","locator":"article body","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary presidential publication describing the summit outcome and the force composition line.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 de-escalation and force-coordination decision.","ruler_attribution":"Directly tied to Tshisekedi's summit participation and the regional security track he backed.","contrary_evidence":["It is official and favorable; it does not by itself prove implementation or civilian protection on the ground."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.7","2B.10"]}

3. Luanda road map and ceasefire logic.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"TRIPARTITE DE LUANDA: JOÂO LOURENCO OBTIENT LA RELANCE DE LA COMMISSION MIXTE RDC- RWANDA","publisher":"Présidence RDC","publication_date":"2022-07-06","url":"https://www.presidence.cd/actualite-detail/actualite/tripartite_de_luanda_joao_lourenco_obtient_la_relance_de_la_commission_mixte_rdc_rwanda","claim":"The Luanda summit agreed on a de-escalation process, normalization of diplomatic relations, immediate cessation of hostilities, and unconditional withdrawal of M23 from occupied positions.","locator":"article body and road-map summary","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary presidential account of a formal summit road map.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 crisis-management decision.","ruler_attribution":"Directly relevant to Tshisekedi as summit participant and signatory to the de-escalation path.","contrary_evidence":["A peace road map is not the same as durable compliance by all armed actors."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.7","2B.10"]}

4. EAC regional force mandate and peacekeeping role.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"East African Community Regional Force (EACRF)","publisher":"East African Community","publication_date":"undated","url":"https://www.eac.int/eac-regional-force","claim":"The EAC says the regional force was deployed in eastern DRC in November 2022 to help restore peace and stability, support civilian protection, and work with FARDC on peace-agreement enforcement and humanitarian access.","locator":"intro section and mandate list","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary regional-institution description of the force's mandate and deployment context.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Describes the force that entered the theater during Tshisekedi's 2022 period.","ruler_attribution":"State/regional framework rather than a personal action record, but it shows the tools Tshisekedi chose to use.","contrary_evidence":["The page is retrospective in tone and does not measure operational success in 2022."],"lenses":["2B.4","2B.7","2B.10"]}

5. Status agreement for the EAC force.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Signature de l'accord portant statut de la force régionale de la CAE pour la paix dans l'est de la RDC","publisher":"Présidence RDC","publication_date":"2022-09-09","url":"https://www.presidence.cd/actualite-detail/actualite/signature_de_laccord_portant_statut_de_la_force_regionale_de_la_cae_pour_la_paix_dans_lest_de_la_rdc","claim":"EAC delegates signed the status agreement for the regional force in Tshisekedi's presence, with the stated purpose of restoring stability, peace, and security in eastern DRC.","locator":"first and second paragraphs","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary presidency report of a formal security agreement signed before the head of state.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 deployment-authorizing step.","ruler_attribution":"Directly tied to Tshisekedi's regional-security choices and venue-setting authority.","contrary_evidence":["Signing an agreement does not prove the force improved outcomes or that all parties complied."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.7","2B.10"]}

6. Civilian harm and rebel conduct in the June-July surge.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"DR Congo: Resurgent M23 Rebels Target Civilians","publisher":"Human Rights Watch","publication_date":"2022-07-25","url":"https://www.hrw.org/news/2022/07/25/dr-congo-resurgent-m23-rebels-target-civilians","claim":"Human Rights Watch said M23 summarily killed at least 29 civilians since mid-June 2022 and warned that the group was likely receiving Rwandan support for its operations in North Kivu.","locator":"opening paragraphs and later sections on killings and alleged support","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Well-documented rights-monitoring report with specific casualty and attribution claims.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 2022 escalation period.","ruler_attribution":"The killings are attributable to M23, not Tshisekedi, but they define the civilian-harm environment and the response challenge.","contrary_evidence":["The Rwandan-support allegation is framed as concern and analysis, not a final legal finding."],"lenses":["2B.4","2B.5","2B.9","2B.10"]}

7. Early displacement shock in North Kivu.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"UNHCR deeply concerned by renewed violence displacing thousands in North Kivu, DR Congo","publisher":"UNHCR","publication_date":"2022-05-27","url":"https://www.unhcr.org/news/briefing-notes/unhcr-deeply-concerned-renewed-violence-displacing-thousands-north-kivu-dr","claim":"UNHCR said more than 72,000 people had been displaced in recent days by fighting in North Kivu, with the broader escalation since November 2021 displacing at least 170,000 civilians.","locator":"opening paragraphs","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary UN humanitarian briefing with a concrete displacement count.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Exact early-2022 crisis baseline.","ruler_attribution":"Inherited humanitarian emergency rather than a ruler-attributed external-war decision.","contrary_evidence":["Humanitarian severity alone does not distinguish Tshisekedi's own contribution from inherited conflict dynamics."],"lenses":["2B.4","2B.10"]}

8. Mid-2022 civilian suffering and attacks.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"UNHCR gravely concerned by death toll of displaced in DR Congo's east","publisher":"UNHCR","publication_date":"2022-07-22","url":"https://www.unhcr.org/news/briefing-notes/unhcr-gravely-concerned-death-toll-displaced-dr-congos-east","claim":"UNHCR warned that eastern DRC civilians were suffering a growing death toll and noted simultaneous armed attacks in Ituri that killed 11 people and burned or looted 250 homes.","locator":"briefing note body","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary UN humanitarian reporting with concrete casualty and destruction figures.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Exact July 2022 escalation period.","ruler_attribution":"This is the harm environment Tshisekedi was trying to manage, not a direct action by him.","contrary_evidence":["UNHCR reports harm and displacement, but not command responsibility for the violence."],"lenses":["2B.4","2B.10"]}

9. Defence-council response, hardening, and continued peace-process commitment.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Communiqué officiel du Conseil Supérieur de la Défense présidé ce samedi 29 octobre 2022 par le Chef de l'État, Félix Tshisekedi","publisher":"Présidence RDC","publication_date":"2022-10-29","url":"https://presidence.cd/actualite-detail/actualite/communique_officiel_du_conseil_superieur_de_la_defense_preside_ce_samedi_29_octobre_2022_par_le_chef_de_letat_felix_tshisekedi","claim":"The defense council said the M23 offensive was backed by the Rwandan army, ordered the government to expel the Rwandan ambassador, increase force posture, send humanitarian aid, and reaffirmed engagement in the Nairobi and Luanda peace processes while warning against hate speech targeting rwandophone communities.","locator":"numbered recommendations in the communiqué","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary government communiqué from a high-level security meeting chaired by the president.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact late-2022 security response.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Tshisekedi's chairing of the council and the decisions announced under his authority.","contrary_evidence":["The communiqué is accusatory and self-justifying; the Rwanda-support claim remained contested in the broader information environment."],"lenses":["2B.5","2B.6","2B.7","2B.9","2B.10"]}

10. National address on the eastern crisis.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Adresse à la nation du Président de la République, Félix Tshisekedi suite à la détérioration de la situation sécuritaire à l’est du pays","publisher":"Présidence RDC","publication_date":"2022-11-03","url":"https://presidence.cd/actualite-detail/actualite/adresse_a_la_nation_du_president_de_la_republique_felix_tshisekedi_suite_a_la_deterioration_de_la_situation_securitaire_a_lest_du_pays","claim":"Tshisekedi told the nation that the M23 was occupying territory in North Kivu with support from Rwanda, said more than 200,000 Congolese had fled, and instructed the government to organize assistance for displaced people.","locator":"opening paragraphs of the address","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary ruler speech with explicit crisis framing and government instructions.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact November 2022 crisis point.","ruler_attribution":"Direct ruler rhetoric and directive in the context of the eastern war.","contrary_evidence":["The address is strongly self-justifying and its external-attribution claims are disputed outside the presidency."],"lenses":["2B.6","2B.7","2B.9","2B.10"]}

11. Luanda mini-summit ceasefire and withdrawal decision.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Le mini-sommet de Luanda impose au m23/Rwanda un cessez-le-feu et le retrait des zones occupées en RDC","publisher":"Présidence RDC","publication_date":"2022-11-24","url":"https://presidence.cd/actualite-detail/actualite/le_mini_sommet_de_luanda_impose_au_m23rwanda_un_cessez_le_feu_et_le_retrait_des_zones_occupees_en_rdc","claim":"The Luanda mini-summit, attended by Tshisekedi and regional leaders, imposed a ceasefire on M23, required withdrawal from occupied areas, linked disarmament and cantonment to the EAC regional force and MONUSCO, and demanded an end to external support for M23.","locator":"article body and quoted communiqué summary","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary presidential report of a signed regional peace decision.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact 23-24 November 2022 peace decision.","ruler_attribution":"Directly relevant to Tshisekedi as summit participant and signatory to the peace framework.","contrary_evidence":["This is a summit outcome, not proof that the ceasefire held or that M23 complied."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.7","2B.10"]}

12. Independent Reuters confirmation of the Luanda ceasefire.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Accord sur un cessez-le-feu dans l'est de la RDC","publisher":"Reuters via Boursorama","publication_date":"2022-11-23","url":"https://www.boursorama.com/actualite-economique/actualites/accord-sur-un-cessez-le-feu-dans-l-est-de-la-rdc-abd0b00c6a2bc6e3cee87abde7569e40","claim":"Reuters reported that African leaders announced a ceasefire in eastern DRC starting Friday and said East African regional forces would intervene against M23 if the truce was not respected.","locator":"lead paragraph and Reuters dateline","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Independent wire reporting syndicated by a major outlet.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact late-November 2022 ceasefire announcement.","ruler_attribution":"Independent confirmation of the regional peace deal Tshisekedi joined.","contrary_evidence":["The report still leaves compliance and effectiveness unresolved."],"lenses":["2B.7","2B.10"]}

13. AU-UN support for the EAC/Nairobi/Luanda track.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Joint Communiqué: Sixth (6th) African Union - United Nations Annual Conference, Addis Ababa, 1st December 2022","publisher":"African Union","publication_date":"2022-12-01","url":"https://au.int/sw/node/42447","claim":"The AU and UN renewed support for the EAC-led peace process and its facilitator, welcomed the Luanda mini-summit final communiqué, and called for its full implementation in eastern DRC.","locator":"paragraph 13 on the Democratic Republic of Congo","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary AU-UN joint communiqué summarizing the formal international peace track.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Exact year-end 2022 peace-process context.","ruler_attribution":"Regional/international endorsement of the peace path Tshisekedi pursued, not a direct presidential act by itself.","contrary_evidence":["International endorsement does not prove implementation or lasting stability on the ground."],"lenses":["2B.7","2B.10"]}

**Search and Rejection Summary**
- I screened roughly 30 documents across presidency releases, AU/EAC pages, UN humanitarian and peacekeeping material, Reuters syndications, and rights-monitoring reports.
- I kept only sources that added distinct value on authority, de-escalation, civilian harm, peace-process steps, or end-state change.
- I rejected repeated coverage of the same June and November peace meetings when the later or independent source added no new factual claim.
- I rejected broad conflict summaries, generic DRC background pages, and later 2023/2024 follow-ups unless they were needed only to describe a 2022 institutional framework.
- I rejected any source that would have duplicated the same peace-process claim without adding a different claim, locator, or source type.
- I did not use the client matrix, and I did not re-fetch the local structured datasets already provided in the prior.

**Remaining Gaps**
- There is still no direct evidence of Tshisekedi personally controlling battlefield conduct, proxy behavior, or FARDC accountability in a way that would resolve all 2B.4/2B.5/2B.9 questions cleanly.
- The record is strong on peace-process participation but weaker on implementation results, especially whether regional agreements materially reduced violence by year-end 2022.
- The most disputed factual point remains Rwanda’s role; the presidency treats it as established, while independent material often frames it as allegation, concern, or contested attribution.
- More search would help mainly on two questions: whether there were verifiable compliance mechanisms for the Luanda/Nairobi agreements, and whether Congolese forces were credibly restrained from abuses during the 2022 campaign.
